  slide "EngineEvent: one construction point, no divergence" {
    eyebrow: "2 · Event model"
    title: "emitted_token cannot diverge from token_id — by construction, not convention"
    lede: "EngineEvent::new is the only place that builds the struct. emitted_token is derived from token_id.is_some(), never set independently, so a caller gating first-token-latency off emitted_token can never desync from the token the event actually carries."
    narration: "Engine event has a private constructor, engine event new, that is the single construction point. The emitted token flag always equals whether a token id is present, because it's derived there, not passed in separately. The terminal status stays authoritative for distinguishing cancellation and failure from successful completion and rejection. Engine event terminal is the second entry point, for a terminal event that carries no output token."
    term: {
      word: "emitted_token"
      meaning: "True exactly when this pass emitted an output token — the caller gates first-token-latency off the first such event. Always equals token_id.is_some(), enforced at construction."
    }
    points: [
      "pub(crate) fn new(uuid, token_id, terminal_status) — the only constructor; fields are not publicly settable.",
      "EngineEvent::terminal(uuid, status) — sugar for new(uuid, None, Some(status)): a terminal event, no token.",
      "terminal_status: Option<ReplayTerminalStatus> distinguishes Completed / Rejected / Canceled / Failed.",
      "event_from_signal() bridges the scheduler's OutputSignal → EngineEvent, deriving Rejected vs Completed from signal.rejected."
    ]
    caption: "struct EngineEvent { uuid, emitted_token, token_id, terminal_status } — one constructor, no divergence."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(id = "s1-hdr", title = "ENGINEEVENT INVARIANT", caption = "single construction point", x = 48.6, y = 43.2, width = 1792.8, height = 118.8, surfaceRole = theme(surface.primary), inkRole = theme(ink.secondary))
      sdk.CodeBlock(
        id = "s1-code",
