  slide "SteppableAgg: multi-worker + KV router" {
    eyebrow: "5 · Aggregated"
    title: "SteppableAgg wraps AggRuntime with defer_drive forced on"
    lede: "AggRuntime::new builds workers.max(1) engines behind a ReplayRouterMode, in ReplayMode::Concurrency { max_in_flight: usize::MAX } so admission is caller-gated, not concurrency-capped by the runtime itself. SteppableAgg::new_with_router_config then sets rt.defer_drive = true before returning — a single field flip that changes the commit ordering of every subsequent step."
    narration: "The aggregated wrapper is a thin shell around one field: an aggregated runtime. Its constructor builds the runtime with an optional KV router config and a prefill load estimator — the same configuration canonical DynoSim replay uses — then unconditionally sets a deferred-drive flag to true. Every trait method after that just forwards: submit calls the runtime's dynamic submit, step calls its dynamic step, and the next-event query calls its own next timestamp. The interesting behavior lives one layer down, in why that deferred-drive flag exists at all."
    term: {
      word: "defer_drive"
      meaning: "AggRuntime flag that switches step_dynamic_until from an atomic single-pass drain to a delta-cycle split — yielding a completion's terminal event before committing the freed slot's replacement, so an externally-submitted replacement lands at the same instant run() would have admitted it in-drain."
    }
    points: [
      "AggRuntime::new(&args, router_config, prefill_load_estimator, VecDeque::new(), workers.max(1), Concurrency{max_in_flight:MAX}, router_mode).",
      "rt.defer_drive = true — set once in the constructor, never toggled per-call.",
      "cluster_in_flight() backs in_flight(); is_workload_done() backs is_idle().",
      "Holds for both RoundRobin and KvRouter: the router's own admission queue is empty at a completion, so the caller's post-yield submit is what actually fills the slot."
    ]
    caption: "workers.max(1) engines + router_mode, Concurrency{MAX}, defer_drive = true."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(id = "s4-hdr", title = "STEPPABLEAGG", caption = "AggRuntime, defer_drive = true", x = 48.6, y = 43.2, width = 1792.8, height = 118.8, surfaceRole = theme(surface.primary), inkRole = theme(ink.secondary))
      sdk.Panel(id = "s4-agg", title = "SteppableAgg { rt: AggRuntime }", detail = "", x = 54, y = 243, width = 810, height = 97.2, surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated), strokeRole = theme(accent.warning))
