  slide "SteppableDisagg: prefill/decode handoff under the same delta cycle" {
    eyebrow: "7 · Disaggregated"
    title: "OfflineDisaggReplayConfig wires two worker pools; defer_drive protects the prefill handoff too"
    lede: "SteppableDisagg::new_with_router_config builds an OfflineDisaggReplayConfig from independent prefill_args/decode_args and prefill_workers.max(1)/decode_workers.max(1), constructs a DisaggRuntime, and forces the identical rt.defer_drive = true — so a freed decode slot's externally-submitted replacement has its prefill driven at the completion instant, not one step late."
    narration: "Disaggregated topology doubles the worker pools — separate engine arguments and separate worker counts for prefill and decode — but the steppable seam is the same shape as the aggregated wrapper: one field, a disaggregated runtime, and the same delta cycle protection. The comment in the source is explicit that this is the prefill handoff being protected: a freed slot's replacement needs its prefill driven at the completion instant, byte-matching the native run loop's in-drain admission, and this holds for both routing modes for the same reason as the aggregated case."
    term: {
      word: "OfflineDisaggReplayConfig"
      meaning: "{ prefill_args, decode_args, num_prefill_workers, num_decode_workers } — the config DisaggRuntime::new consumes to build independent prefill and decode worker pools behind one router."
    }
    points: [
      "Two independent MockEngineArgs: prefill_args and decode_args — different engine configuration per stage.",
      "prefill_workers.max(1), decode_workers.max(1) — independently sized pools.",
      "The only difference from SteppableAgg's constructor: an extra config struct and a second worker pool; defer_drive, router_config, and prefill_load_estimator plumbing are identical in shape.",
      "cov_steppable_engine.rs::disaggregated_events_expose_only_collector_visible_decode_tokens verifies emitted_token count equals report.request_counts.total_output_tokens — the caller only ever sees decode-visible tokens."
    ]
    caption: "prefill pool + decode pool + router, same defer_drive discipline as SteppableAgg."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(id = "s6-hdr", title = "STEPPABLEDISAGG", caption = "prefill/decode, same delta cycle", x = 48.6, y = 43.2, width = 1792.8, height = 118.8, surfaceRole = theme(surface.primary), inkRole = theme(ink.secondary))
